1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
codsh. One sentence, to verified code.
DeepSeek — or any compatible endpoint.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Type /ship, then your sentence.
This one: open long diffs in a pager instead of scrolling past.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
It reads the repo first, then asks the one choice still open.
Full screen, or split. It recommends full screen. You answer once.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,000
The spec writes itself. Six acceptance checks,
each with a command that must exit 0. Gate 1. You confirm.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000
The work splits into three independently provable tickets.
You approve. Baseline runs. Red stays red.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Then it lands red to green.
Each ticket that turns green is one clean commit. One. Two. Three.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Every proof command runs again against the baseline.
Zero new failures. Dual-layer done. Now you can merge it back.

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Two commands. npm i -g @deepseek-ai/dsh codsh-cli
Then codsh. Key: DEEPSEEK_API_KEY.
